  "changes": [
    "assessment_items.json: WA-F02 and WB-F02 no longer carry VG_NEGATION, WA-D01 no longer carries VG_LOCATION, and WB-D01 no longer carries VG_GENDER_NUMBER. Each keeps its W_SENTENCE or W_DESCRIPTION skill and its version goes to 2. A grammar skill cannot be evidenced from the generic writing rubric: its dimensions are message, vocabulary, structure, conventions and independence, so a child writing 'Je deteste le fromage' scores well on message and structure while demonstrating no negation. All three skills remain measured by the vocabulary and grammar section's own items. Target-specific criteria and matched prompts on both forms would be a Release B change, not a rubric reading.",
    "No rule, rubric, fixture, threshold, prompt, answer key or model response changed."
  ]
